<title>USA: Community Financial Corp Q1. [CORRECTED 23:58 GMT 15/5]</title>
<headline>Community Financial Corp Q1. [CORRECTED 23:58 GMT 15/5]</headline>
<dateline>OLNEY, Ill. 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Company corrects the interest income, net interest income, net interest income after provision for loan losses, total noninterest income and total noninterest expense figures.) </p>
<p>		     (Dollars in thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>							 Three Months Ended</p>
<p>								 March 31,</p>
<p>							 1997	    1996</p>
<p> Interest Income*			     $  3,502     $  3,455</p>
<p> Interest Expense				  1,690	  1,693</p>
<p> Net Interest Income*			    1,812	  1,762</p>
<p> Provision for loan losses			  33	  ( 51)</p>
<p>Net interest income</p>
<p>   after provision*				1,779	  1,813</p>
<p> Total noninterest income*			 222	    197</p>
<p> Total noninterest expense*		    1,937	  1,318</p>
<p>Income before federal</p>
<p>   income tax provision			     64	    692</p>
<p> Federal income tax				   22	    248</p>
<p> Net Income					     42	    444</p>
<p>Per share earnings on</p>
<p>   common stock				     0.02	   0.19</p>
<p>NOTE: Company said decline in Q1 1997 net income due primarily to early retirement program, which was accepted by seven employees during the quarter.</p>
<p>(* Company corrects)</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
